ODEL","type":"MODEL","links":[151]}],"title":"Unet Loader (GGUF) - Low Noise","properties":{"cnr_id":"comfyui-gguf","ver":"1.1.10","Node name for S&R":"UnetLoaderGGUF","ue_properties":{"widget_ue_connectable":{},"input_ue_unconnectable":{},"version":"7.8"}},"widgets_values":["Wan2.2-I2V-A14B-LowNoise-Q4_K_M.gguf"],"ndSuperSelectorEnabled":false,"ndPowerEnabled":false},{"id":32,"type":"Note","pos":[1901.0791004076027,729.3075523756977],"size":[507.1764705882356,1078.6666666666667],"flags":{},"order":5,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"title":"Workflow Notes","properties":{"ue_properties":{"widget_ue_connectable":{},"version":"7.8","input_ue_unconnectable":{}}},"widgets_values":["Workflow Goal:\n\nProvide a clean reference implementation for WAN based image-to-video generation.\n\nThis workflow focuses on simplicity, reproducibility, and education rather than including every available feature. It reflects a tested baseline for producing high-quality videos from a starting frame. Treat it as a starting point and adapt the prompt and LoRA stack for your preferred artistic direction.\n\nIMPORTANT NOTE:\n\nValidated using an NVIDIA RTX 2080 (8 GB VRAM) with 64 GB System RAM.\n\nLow VRAM does not mean low hardware requirements.\n\nWAN 2.2 Image-to-Video is computationally intensive. Even when GPU VRAM is managed efficiently, higher resolutions and longer videos can require substantial system RAM for memory paging and intermediate data.\n\n⚠️ Hardware & Resolution Notes\n\n\nWhile the workflow is designed to be 8 GB VRAM friendly, the available 64 GB of system RAM also helped accommodate memory-intensive operations.\n\nIf your system has:\n\n8 GB VRAM + 16 GB RAM, expect slower generation speeds or possible out-of-memory errors.\n8 GB VRAM + 32 GB RAM, results should be closer but still depend on your operating system and background memory usage.\n8 GB VRAM + 64 GB RAM (or more), you are more likely to reproduce the results achieved during\n\n----------------------------------------------------\n\nVersion 1.0\n\nCreated as a simple reference workflow for users getting started with WAN Video generation.\n\n\nPurpose\n\n✓ Educational\n✓ Minimal\n✓ Easy to extend\n\nVerified\n\n✓ Image-to-Video\n\nVerified Settings\n\n✓ CFG : 1.0\n✓ Steps : 4 (2 High + 2 Low)\n✓ 81 Frames (5 seconds @ 16 fps)\n✓ Sampler : Euler\n✓ Scheduler : sgm_uniform\n\nThese settings were used to validate this workflow and are recommended as the baseline configuration.\n\nVerified Resolution (MAX):\n✓ 480p\n\n\nHardware Tested:\n\n✓ RTX 2080 (8 GB)\n✓ 64 GB System RAM\n✓ ComfyUI 0.27.0\n\nNext\n\n□ Text-to-Video"],"color":"#323","bgcolor":"#535"},{"id":33,"type":"Note","pos":[2423.020276878193,721.4251994345211],"size":[527.4705882352941,1086.549019607843],"flags":{},"order":6,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"title":"Resources","properties":{"ue_properties":{"widget_ue_connectable":{},"version":"7.8","input_ue_unconnectable":{}}},"widgets_values":["Model used in this workflow:\n\nModel\n• WAN2.2-I2V-A14B-HighNoise-Q4_K_M.gguf\n• WAN2.2-I2V-A14B-LowNoise-Q4_K_M.gguf\n\nText Encoder\n• umt5-xxl-encoder-Q3_K_M\n\nVAE\n• wan_2.1_vae\n\nLoRA\n\n• wan2.2_i2v_A14b_high_noise_lora_rank64_lightx2v_4step_1022\n• wan2.2_i2v_A14b_low_noise_lora_rank64_lightx2v_4step_1022\n• Compatible with WAN LoRAs\n\n\n----------------------------------------------------\n\nPerformance Note\n\nThis workflow is validated using the Lightx2v Lightning LoRAs.\nDuring testing on an RTX 2080 (8 GB), enabling these LoRAs reduced generation time significantly compared to the non-Lightning configuration while maintaining comparable visual quality.\n\nWithout lightning loras, i tested with CFG = 6 ;  20 Steps - 12 high and 8 low. It took a very long time to generate the same video. With the lora, my average generation time is ~500 seconds\n\n\n----------------------------------------------------\n\n\nCredits\n\n• Thanks to the original developers for creating these excellent models and tools."],"col